WEBVTT

00:00:00.343 --> 00:00:02.340
Last video ended with this question.

00:00:03.025 --> 00:00:05.541
Mark one sigma either side of the mean.

00:00:06.287 --> 00:00:08.520
How much of the area lies between those

00:00:08.602 --> 00:00:08.923
marks?

00:00:10.029 --> 00:00:12.818
This curve has no simple area formula, so

00:00:12.859 --> 00:00:15.407
today a graphing calculator does the measuring.

00:00:16.431 --> 00:00:18.915
An orchard grades its apples by mass, and

00:00:18.936 --> 00:00:21.419
the masses are normal, with mean one hundred

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:24.285
and fifty grams and standard deviation fifteen.

00:00:25.108 --> 00:00:26.851
Then we'll turn what we find into a

00:00:26.952 --> 00:00:29.437
rule you can use with no technology at

00:00:29.478 --> 00:00:29.617
all.

00:00:31.121 --> 00:00:34.095
This is the normal probability density function, and

00:00:34.195 --> 00:00:35.160
each part has a job.

00:00:35.903 --> 00:00:38.248
The power of e is minus the squared

00:00:38.309 --> 00:00:40.974
distance from the mean, over two sigma squared.

00:00:41.556 --> 00:00:43.601
The same distance either side squares to the

00:00:43.642 --> 00:00:45.766
same value, so the curve is symmetric.

00:00:46.489 --> 00:00:48.579
Further out, the power gets more negative,

00:00:49.122 --> 00:00:50.749
so the curve drops towards zero.

00:00:51.394 --> 00:00:54.167
But e to any power is positive, so

00:00:54.228 --> 00:00:55.312
it never reaches the axis.

00:00:56.257 --> 00:00:58.203
The number in front makes the total area

00:00:58.404 --> 00:00:59.166
exactly one.

00:00:59.909 --> 00:01:02.316
For the apples, two sigma squared is four

00:01:02.377 --> 00:01:03.239
hundred and fifty.

00:01:03.821 --> 00:01:04.928
Where's the highest point?

00:01:05.711 --> 00:01:07.916
By the chain rule, f prime of x

00:01:08.097 --> 00:01:10.522
is the derivative of the power, times f

00:01:10.562 --> 00:01:11.244
of x itself.

00:01:11.865 --> 00:01:14.309
Since f of x is always positive, the

00:01:14.411 --> 00:01:16.835
sign of the gradient comes from minus x

00:01:16.896 --> 00:01:17.396
minus mu.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:20.331
Left of the mean the gradient is positive,

00:01:20.533 --> 00:01:21.397
so the curve rises.

00:01:21.983 --> 00:01:23.634
Right of the mean it's negative, so the

00:01:23.655 --> 00:01:24.279
curve falls.

00:01:25.064 --> 00:01:26.984
It rises all the way to mu and

00:01:27.025 --> 00:01:29.826
falls all the way after, so x equals

00:01:29.907 --> 00:01:32.347
mu is the global maximum, not just a

00:01:32.368 --> 00:01:32.828
local one.

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:35.877
Its height is one over sigma root two

00:01:35.939 --> 00:01:36.179
pi.

00:01:36.862 --> 00:01:38.089
Now the points of inflection.

00:01:38.792 --> 00:01:41.761
Differentiate again with the product rule, and factorise.

00:01:42.584 --> 00:01:44.512
Again f of x is positive, so the

00:01:44.573 --> 00:01:46.721
sign of the second derivative comes from this

00:01:46.803 --> 00:01:47.103
bracket.

00:01:47.787 --> 00:01:50.134
It's zero when the quantity x minus mu,

00:01:50.234 --> 00:01:52.240
squared, equals sigma squared,

00:01:52.883 --> 00:01:54.588
so at mu plus or minus sigma.

00:01:55.471 --> 00:01:58.036
Between those points the bracket is negative, so

00:01:58.057 --> 00:02:00.260
the curve is concave down, like a cap

00:02:00.402 --> 00:02:00.842
over the peak.

00:02:01.705 --> 00:02:04.159
Outside them it's concave up, and the tails

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:04.662
flatten out.

00:02:05.427 --> 00:02:07.831
The concavity changes, so these are points of

00:02:07.872 --> 00:02:10.778
inflection, at one thirty-five and one sixty-five.

00:02:11.382 --> 00:02:13.535
So one sigma is where the bell changes

00:02:13.636 --> 00:02:14.018
its bend.

00:02:14.583 --> 00:02:15.250
Back to the question.

00:02:15.854 --> 00:02:17.803
Ask the calculator for the area from one

00:02:17.823 --> 00:02:19.551
thirty-five to one sixty-five.

00:02:20.174 --> 00:02:22.003
It works out the area numerically:

00:02:22.606 --> 00:02:24.395
zero point six eight two seven.

00:02:25.017 --> 00:02:27.224
So in the model, about sixty-eight percent of

00:02:27.284 --> 00:02:29.130
apples land within one sigma.

00:02:30.011 --> 00:02:32.115
Widen the band to two sigma and it

00:02:32.155 --> 00:02:34.599
gives zero point nine five four five,

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:37.665
and three sigma gives zero point nine nine

00:02:37.745 --> 00:02:38.366
seven three.

00:02:39.269 --> 00:02:40.773
If you use a calculator or app in

00:02:40.794 --> 00:02:42.178
an answer, say that you did.

00:02:43.022 --> 00:02:44.089
Is that just these apples?

00:02:44.632 --> 00:02:47.217
Try last video's chip bags, with mean one

00:02:47.258 --> 00:02:49.843
seventy-five grams and standard deviation four.

00:02:50.746 --> 00:02:53.657
From one seventy-one to one seventy-nine, the calculator

00:02:53.677 --> 00:02:56.288
gives zero point six eight two seven again.

00:02:57.241 --> 00:02:57.669
Here's why.

00:02:58.294 --> 00:03:00.330
Changing mu slides the bell along.

00:03:00.692 --> 00:03:03.697
Changing sigma stretches it sideways and squashes it

00:03:03.738 --> 00:03:06.101
down by the same factor, so the area

00:03:06.142 --> 00:03:08.164
between matching marks doesn't change.

00:03:09.167 --> 00:03:10.891
Measured in sigmas from the mean,

00:03:11.434 --> 00:03:13.319
every normal curve is the same curve.

00:03:14.149 --> 00:03:15.275
That's the empirical rule.

00:03:15.698 --> 00:03:19.082
For any normal distribution, approximately sixty-eight percent of

00:03:19.103 --> 00:03:21.685
the data lie within one standard deviation of

00:03:21.706 --> 00:03:22.046
the mean,

00:03:22.647 --> 00:03:24.969
approximately ninety-five percent within two,

00:03:25.531 --> 00:03:28.694
and approximately ninety-nine point seven percent within three.

00:03:29.497 --> 00:03:32.743
They're approximate, because the calculator gave sixty-eight point

00:03:32.784 --> 00:03:33.906
two seven, and so on.

00:03:34.712 --> 00:03:35.884
Symmetry gives the tails.

00:03:36.631 --> 00:03:39.998
Outside one sigma is thirty-two percent, so sixteen

00:03:40.039 --> 00:03:41.001
percent in each tail.

00:03:41.684 --> 00:03:43.850
Outside two sigma, two and a half percent

00:03:43.911 --> 00:03:44.351
each side.

00:03:45.155 --> 00:03:47.963
Outside three sigma, zero point one five percent

00:03:48.064 --> 00:03:48.525
each side.

00:03:49.255 --> 00:03:51.839
Heights of Year 12 students are normal, with

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:55.106
mean one seventy centimetres and standard deviation eight.

00:03:55.849 --> 00:03:58.463
What percentage are between one sixty-two and one

00:03:58.545 --> 00:03:59.047
seventy-eight?

00:03:59.752 --> 00:04:02.729
That's eight either side, one sigma, so about

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:03.594
sixty-eight percent.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:06.793
What percentage are taller than one eighty-six?

00:04:07.619 --> 00:04:09.875
That's two eights above, so two sigma.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:13.025
Outside two sigma is five percent, and half

00:04:13.046 --> 00:04:15.131
of that is above, so about two point

00:04:15.172 --> 00:04:15.712
five percent.

00:04:16.255 --> 00:04:17.802
The rule also helps you judge.

00:04:18.506 --> 00:04:21.714
Is a student of one ninety-six centimetres unusual?

00:04:22.658 --> 00:04:24.985
Three sigma above is one ninety-four.

00:04:25.729 --> 00:04:28.138
Only about zero point one five percent are

00:04:28.179 --> 00:04:30.768
above that, so even fewer are above one

00:04:30.809 --> 00:04:31.270
ninety-six.

00:04:32.034 --> 00:04:32.860
Very unusual.

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:34.939
Now the small apples.

00:04:35.767 --> 00:04:37.960
Apples under one hundred and thirty grams go

00:04:38.001 --> 00:04:38.423
to juice.

00:04:39.248 --> 00:04:41.794
One thirty sits between one sigma below and

00:04:41.915 --> 00:04:42.837
two sigma below.

00:04:43.319 --> 00:04:45.710
So that tail is between two point five

00:04:45.872 --> 00:04:47.076
and sixteen percent.

00:04:47.881 --> 00:04:49.706
For an actual value, we need the area

00:04:49.788 --> 00:04:51.332
to the left of one thirty.

00:04:52.156 --> 00:04:54.142
That's the cumulative distribution function.

00:04:54.605 --> 00:04:56.933
Capital F of x is the probability that

00:04:57.215 --> 00:04:58.699
X is at most x,

00:04:59.202 --> 00:05:00.706
the area to the left of x.

00:05:01.531 --> 00:05:03.503
Graph it on the calculator, and it draws

00:05:03.524 --> 00:05:04.448
an S shape.

00:05:05.153 --> 00:05:07.299
It starts near zero, and at the mean

00:05:07.421 --> 00:05:09.869
it's exactly a half, because half the area

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:10.571
is on each side.

00:05:11.355 --> 00:05:13.780
Its slope is the density, so it climbs

00:05:13.901 --> 00:05:16.186
fastest at mu, where the bell is highest.

00:05:16.748 --> 00:05:18.261
Then it levels off towards one.

00:05:19.169 --> 00:05:21.810
At one thirty, the calculator reads zero point

00:05:21.911 --> 00:05:24.592
zero nine one two, so the model says

00:05:24.653 --> 00:05:26.193
about nine percent go to juice.

00:05:26.861 --> 00:05:28.128
Here's a way to remember the rule.

00:05:28.992 --> 00:05:29.554
Sixty-eight,

00:05:30.055 --> 00:05:30.677
ninety-five,

00:05:31.219 --> 00:05:32.322
ninety-nine point seven,

00:05:32.924 --> 00:05:33.345
for one,

00:05:33.906 --> 00:05:35.511
two and three sigma.

00:05:36.313 --> 00:05:39.158
And for a tail, find what's outside, then

00:05:39.259 --> 00:05:39.659
halve it.

00:05:42.387 --> 00:05:42.796
Your turn.

00:05:43.385 --> 00:05:44.490
Use the empirical rule.

00:05:44.953 --> 00:05:45.918
Pause here to answer.

00:05:56.568 --> 00:05:59.376
The second number is the variance, so sigma

00:05:59.457 --> 00:05:59.917
is six.

00:06:00.701 --> 00:06:03.828
Sixty-eight and ninety-two are twelve either side of

00:06:03.889 --> 00:06:05.432
eighty, which is two sigma.

00:06:05.934 --> 00:06:08.393
So that probability is about ninety-five percent.

00:06:09.118 --> 00:06:11.104
Eighty-six is one sigma above.

00:06:12.068 --> 00:06:15.710
Outside one sigma is thirty-two percent, and half

00:06:15.731 --> 00:06:18.192
of that is above, so about sixteen percent.

00:06:19.317 --> 00:06:20.483
Thirty-two percent is wrong.

00:06:20.786 --> 00:06:21.919
That counts both tails.

00:06:23.836 --> 00:06:24.327
Last one.

00:06:24.893 --> 00:06:26.726
Read the features from the formula.

00:06:27.252 --> 00:06:28.362
Pause here to answer.

00:06:38.968 --> 00:06:40.354
Match it to the general formula.

00:06:41.178 --> 00:06:42.340
The mean is forty,

00:06:42.882 --> 00:06:44.906
and the number in front has five where

00:06:44.947 --> 00:06:46.950
sigma goes, so sigma is five.

00:06:47.813 --> 00:06:50.394
The global maximum is at x equals forty,

00:06:50.796 --> 00:06:53.317
with height one over five root two pi.

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:56.709
The points of inflection are one sigma either

00:06:56.771 --> 00:06:59.059
side, at thirty-five and forty-five.

00:06:59.924 --> 00:07:02.160
Forty plus or minus root fifty is wrong.

00:07:02.685 --> 00:07:05.624
Fifty is two sigma squared, not sigma squared.

00:07:07.248 --> 00:07:09.491
So the calculator shows where the curve peaks

00:07:09.633 --> 00:07:10.113
and bends,

00:07:10.615 --> 00:07:13.680
verifies the empirical rule, and graphs the CDF.

00:07:14.405 --> 00:07:15.692
Next, a new question.

00:07:16.315 --> 00:07:20.002
A forty-five centimetre snapper is five centimetres above

00:07:20.044 --> 00:07:21.827
the average snapper off one jetty.

00:07:22.509 --> 00:07:25.477
A forty centimetre golden perch is four above

00:07:25.498 --> 00:07:27.001
the average perch in one river.

00:07:27.724 --> 00:07:30.257
Which catch is more unusual, and how much

00:07:30.419 --> 00:07:31.544
area lies beyond each?

00:07:34.215 --> 00:07:34.997
Here are the key notes.

00:07:35.581 --> 00:07:36.968
Pause the video if you need more time

00:07:37.009 --> 00:07:37.471
to copy them.
